[/list][h2]Void Sword[/h2]The Void Sword is added directly to the operator creative tab as a separate item.
It is internally based on a netherite sword but uses the diamond sword item model.
[h3]Display[/h3][list]
[*]Name: [b]Void Sword[/b][/*]
[*]Name color: Light purple[/*]
[*]Name style: Bold[/*]
[*]Item model: Diamond Sword[/*]
[*]Enchantment glint: Always enabled[/*]
[*]Unbreakable[/*]
[/list][h3]Damage Behavior[/h3]The sword uses the [b]fell_out_of_world[/b] damage type.
This is the damage type associated with void damage rather than normal melee damage.
[h3]Attributes[/h3]When held in either hand, the sword provides:
[list]
[*]Attack Damage: +2,147,483,647[/*]
[*]Attack Speed: +2,147,483,647[/*]
[/list][h3]Range[/h3][list]
[*]Maximum configured attack range: 64 blocks[/*]
[*]Maximum configured creative attack range: 64 blocks[/*]
[/list][h3]Blocking[/h3]The sword also receives the same all-damage blocking component used by the administrator shield:
[list]
[*]Blocks every registered damage type[/*]
[*]Uses a 360-degree blocking angle[/*]
[*]Uses zero blocking delay[/*]
[*]Takes no durability damage while blocking[/*]
[*]Applies a very high damage-reduction value[/*]
[/list]Actual behavior remains subject to server-side item validation and combat authority.
[h2]Glideplate Compatibility[/h2]Each shulker box includes a specially configured netherite chestplate with Elytra functionality.
The chestplate includes:
[list]
[*][b]glideplate_has_elytra[/b] custom data[/*]
[*][b]gliding[/b] custom data[/*]
[*][b]gliding_chestplate_has_elytra[/b] custom data[/*]
[*]Glideplate-compatible custom model data[/*]
[*]The vanilla glider component[/*]
[*]The translated name [b]Netherite Chestplate with Elytra[/b][/*]
[*]The lore text [b]With Elytra[/b][/*]
[/list]These components allow the item to behave as a gliding chestplate without registering a new item type.
The generated chestplate uses compatibility data associated with [url=https://modrinth.com/mod/glideplate]Glideplate[/url].
Installing Glideplate may improve the related item names, models, and visual presentation, but Best Armor generates the item stacks directly.
[h2]Creative Tab Behavior[/h2]The generated items are added to the operator creative tab only when operator-restricted items are visible.
The following items are added to both the main operator-tab display and creative inventory search:
[list]
[*]Yellow Shulker Box[/*]
[*]Orange Shulker Box[/*]
[*]Red Shulker Box[/*]
[*]Void Sword[/*]
[/list]The items are generated only when a client world is available because the mod requires the active registry access to resolve enchantments and damage types.
[h2]Technical Behavior[/h2]Best Armor directly creates [b]ItemStack[/b] instances and assigns vanilla data components.
The mod uses components including:
[list]
[*]Enchantments[/*]
[*]Unbreakable[/*]
[*]Attribute Modifiers[/*]
[*]Container Contents[/*]
[*]Custom Data[/*]
[*]Custom Model Data[/*]
[*]Glider[/*]
[*]Item Name[/*]
[*]Item Lore[/*]
[*]Attack Range[/*]
[*]Blocks Attacks[/*]
[*]Damage Type[/*]
[*]Enchantment Glint Override[/*]
[*]Item Model[/*]
[/list]The mod does not:
[list]
[*]Register custom item types[/*]
[*]Register custom blocks[/*]
[*]Register commands[/*]
[*]Add configuration files[/*]
[*]Add screens[/*]
[*]Read item definitions from JSON or text files[/*]
[*]Execute [b]/give[/b] commands[/*]
[*]Parse command strings[/*]
[/list][h2]Visual Behavior[/h2][list]
[*]The yellow, orange, and red boxes appear as vanilla colored shulker boxes[/*]
[*]Each box uses a custom item name[/*]
[*]The three boxes appear in the operator creative tab and creative search[/*]
[*]The Void Sword uses the diamond sword model[/*]
[*]The Void Sword always displays an enchantment glint[/*]
[*]Glideplate-style chestplates include custom naming, lore, and model data[/*]
[*]No custom textures are included by this mod[/*]
[*]No custom user interface or HUD is added[/*]
[/list][h2]Multiplayer Safety[/h2][list]
[*]Client-side only[/*]
[*]No server installation is required for the mod itself to load[/*]
[*]Server authority still controls inventory and combat behavior[/*]
[*]Servers may validate, alter, reject, or remove generated item stacks[/*]
[*]Unsupported enchantment combinations may behave inconsistently across servers[/*]
[*]Custom attributes and data components may be rejected by server-side validation[/*]
[*]The Void Sword and administrator equipment can severely disrupt normal gameplay[/*]
[*]Use these items only in private worlds or on servers where administrator equipment is explicitly allowed[/*]
[/list][h2]Supported Versions[/h2][list]
[*]Minecraft 26.1.2[/*]
[*]Fabric Loader 0.19.2+[/*]
[*]Fabric API 0.150.0+[/*]
[*]Java 25[/*]
[/list][h2]License[/h2]MIT
